Theorem RL-22: KnownSafe inner-pair elimination (physical RC provably positive)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-22 governs KnownSafe pair elimination per Annex E §AIMS
      KnownSafe Pair Elimination: when the physical RC is provably positive
      (a dominating RcInc in scope with no intervening RcDec), inner
      RcInc/RcDec pairs on the same variable SHALL be eliminated. KnownSafe(v)
      = true at a point when there exists a dominating RcInc with no
      intervening RcDec.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-22 is a POST-PIPELINE pass operating on realized IR (Swift ARC
      optimizer lineage per Annex E §AIMS §8); VF-7
      tier (a)+(b)+(c) applies when implemented.
    - Transfer: RcInc(v) -> KnownSafe(v) := true; RcDec(v) -> KnownSafe(v) :=
      false for v and all SSA / borrow aliases; Set/SetTag and may_deallocate
      calls -> false.

  Soundness property:
    Forall variable v with an inner RcInc/RcDec pair at a point P:

      (P1) Elimination decision: RL-22 eliminates the inner pair iff
           KnownSafe(v) at P — i.e. a dominating RcInc with no intervening
           RcDec (physical RC >= 2).

      (P2) RC-count preservation: when KnownSafe, physical RC >= 2, so the
           inner RcDec cannot reach 0 (cannot free); removing the matched
           inner inc+dec pair is net-0 on the balance ledger — the lifecycle
           with the inner pair and the lifecycle with it eliminated both
           balance to RC 0.

    RL-22 refines plain ARC by removing redundant inc/dec pairs the dominating
    inc makes unnecessary, with no change to the observable RC balance.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1) — KnownSafe decision grid:
      dominating_inc_no_dec_eliminate -> KnownSafe (eliminate)
      intervening_dec_keep_pair -> NOT KnownSafe (RC may be 1; keep)
      no_dominating_inc_keep_pair -> NOT KnownSafe (keep)
      Coverage gate: 3 decisions.

    Part (P2) — net-0 balance preservation:
      The verifier asserts the with-inner-pair lifecycle ([alloc, outer inc,
      inner inc, inner dec, outer dec, final dec]) and the eliminated
      lifecycle ([alloc, outer inc, outer dec, final dec]) both net to 0 on
      the RC ledger. Negative-direction witness: pair elimination must NOT
      fire without a dominating inc (RC may be 1, so the inner dec could free
      a still-referenced value) — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl22_knownsafe_pair_elimination; KnownSafe decision
        grid + net-0 ledger preservation; emits Fail on a wrong decision or a
        balance violation)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-22 via the KnownSafe decision grid (dominating inc + no intervening dec -> eliminate) and net-0 RC-ledger preservation showing the with-inner-pair and eliminated lifecycles both balance, with a negative-direction witness rejecting elimination without a dominating inc, grounded in the Swift ARC KnownSafe lineage (Annex E §AIMS §8)
